	quests: [
		{
			dependencies: [
				"690A67A6D21199B1"
			]
			description: [
				"Create's own shafts, cogs, gearboxes and machines are the andesite tier. They never weather and their shafts take any load, but their supports stop at 128 RPM."
				""
				"Andesite stays the maintenance-free workhorse for slow, heavy machines all game."
			]
			id: "541D0DC718F4FF4B"
			rewards: [ ]
			subtitle: "Create's own tier, steady and slow"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "4486CF6DB0698A53"
					item: "create:andesite_alloy"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "Andesite Alloy"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"541D0DC718F4FF4B"
			]
			description: [
				"A bare shaft or cog can't hang in the air. It must be held by a support: a machine, a gearbox, clutch, gearshift or chain drive, a casing, or a bracket bolted to a solid block. Water wheels, windmills and engines pass rotation on but hold nothing."
				""
				"A support holds the parts in line with it as far as their own material reaches, counting through the bare parts between, like scaffolding from a post: two blocks for wood and brass, four for andesite, copper and iron, six for steel and up. Out of reach a part won't go on, and when its support goes it drops."
				""
				"&7Ponder: any shaft, bracket or casing.&r"
			]
			id: "629C0AF66AEA3D00"
			rewards: [ ]
			subtitle: "Every part turns in a support"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "17E6F1B412B0AFFE"
					item: "create:shaft"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "Shafts Need Holding"
			x: 1.75d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"629C0AF66AEA3D00"
				"3AC9A7994C4F9DC0"
			]
			description: [
				"Create's Engineer's Goggles show what a placed block is doing: each part's material, what holds it and its limits, a Furnace's heat and fuel, and what a machine is waiting for."
				""
				"Their lenses sit in gold sheet, and sheets come only off a press, so goggles wait for iron."
			]
			id: "48EF2BB3E8E92849"
			rewards: [ ]
			subtitle: "See what a block is doing"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "54288B7E7E69C060"
					item: "create:goggles"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "Engineer's Goggles"
			x: 1.75d
			y: -1.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"629C0AF66AEA3D00"
			]
			description: [
				"Each material gives two limits. A support's Stability is the top speed it turns at. A shaft or cog's Strength is the load it carries. A part turns as fast as its supports allow, whatever it is made of."
				""
				"Spin a support past its Stability and it grinds for a few seconds, then gives way and drops. Draw more stress through a network than a shaft or cog can carry and it wobbles, then breaks. Supports never break from load, and shafts never break from speed."
				""
				"Tooltips show both as a word and a bar, and goggles give the numbers."
			]
			icon: "create:stressometer"
			id: "3296CE900D1C9370"
			rewards: [ ]
			subtitle: "Speed breaks supports, load breaks shafts"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "621F22D461AC08AE"
					title: "Got it"
					type: "checkmark"
				}
			]
			title: "Stability and Strength"
			x: 3.5d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"629C0AF66AEA3D00"
			]
			description: [
				"Logs make wooden shafts cheaply, and every one of the eleven woods has its own parts. Wood is the cheapest tier: its supports stop at 64 RPM, and its shafts carry the least load of anything."
				""
				"That makes a wooden shaft a fuse. Between an engine and a risky machine, it is the first thing to break when the machine draws too much."
				""
				"Crimson and warped parts don't burn."
			]
			id: "0BBD389261D0567C"
			optional: true
			rewards: [ ]
			subtitle: "The cheapest parts give way first"
			tasks: [
				{
					icon: "mcremix:oak_shaft"
					id: "3B852AEACAF79693"
					observe_type: 1
					timer: 10L
					title: "Look at a wooden shaft"
					to_observe: "#mcremix:wooden_shafts"
					type: "observation"
				}
			]
			title: "Wood Is the Fuse"
			x: 3.5d
			y: -1.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"3296CE900D1C9370"
			]
			description: [
				"Copper supports turn up to 256 RPM, twice andesite's, and copper shafts and cogs carry light loads. They are the early road to full-speed lines."
				""
				"Copper weathers anywhere, within a day, and each stage adds a little friction at its supports. Honeycomb waxes it and an axe scrapes it back, just like copper blocks."
				""
				"Copper gearboxes, clutches, gearshifts and chain drives are built on Create's copper casing."
			]
			id: "2D5A296BEAA4D578"
			rewards: [ ]
			subtitle: "Full speed, light duty"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "218168076A2D4D86"
					item: "mcremix:copper_shaft"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "Copper Parts"
			x: 5.25d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"2D5A296BEAA4D578"
				"4718C7B7C98B7081"
			]
			description: [
				"Copper and iron weather fast and stop at a stage of their own: each spot ends weathered or fully weathered, so a build takes on a varied palette within a day of play instead of one flat green."
				""
				"Iron only rusts while wet: rained on, waterlogged or beside water. Dry iron under rustier iron rusts too, so rust runs down a wall as far as the blocks above it got. Indoor machines stay clean."
				""
				"Honeycomb seals a block as it is. An axe scrapes it back a stage, and it weathers to the same stage again."
			]
			id: "060ABCEC2D22B788"
			optional: true
			rewards: [ ]
			subtitle: "Fast, and never quite all the way"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "2E7BA13AA358CDF3"
					item: "minecraft:honeycomb"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "Weathering"
			x: 7.0d
			y: -1.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"2D5A296BEAA4D578"
				"5CF0F2FE999D2187"
				"3AC9A7994C4F9DC0"
			]
			description: [
				"A Create basin standing on a Furnace is heated by the fuel burning in it, for the mixer or press above. Fuel burning &cSearing&r heats it as a fed Blaze Burner does, which is enough for heated mixing such as brass; a &eWarm&r or &6Hot&r fire only warms it. Heat from under the Furnace passes up as it is, so a soul campfire beneath only warms the basin."
				""
				"Superheated recipes still need a Blaze Burner fed Blaze Cake, later Power Grid's basin heater run hot enough, or a Steel Furnace burning &bBlazing&r."
			]
			id: "36D4E952BA3CE9EC"
			rewards: [ ]
			subtitle: "A heated basin, no blazes needed"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "502A8E24B52D373D"
					item: "create:brass_ingot"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "Brass"
			x: 7.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"36D4E952BA3CE9EC"
			]
			description: [
				"Brass parts are fine clockwork, polished and delicate. Their supports stop at 96 RPM and their shafts carry little, just above wood, because brass already has some powerful machines."
				""
				"Brass never tarnishes. It has no clutch, gearshift or chain gearshift, and the Mechanical Crafter comes only in brass."
			]
			id: "15A0CEE9BF75BD3A"
			rewards: [ ]
			subtitle: "Delicate and fancy"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "5906A2B49E2162C7"
					item: "mcremix:brass_cogwheel"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "Clockwork Brass"
			x: 8.75d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"2D5A296BEAA4D578"
			]
			description: [
				"Create's press, mixer, millstone, fan, saw, drill, deployer and arm also come in copper, iron, steel, aluminium and titanium. Each is the same machine in another casing, a support held to its own metal's top speed."
				""
				"Use a casing on a placed machine to change its metal, up or down. It keeps its facing and settings, and the old casing pops out."
				""
				"&7Ponder: any machine shows the materials scene.&r"
			]
			id: "20B01B5CDC744C67"
			rewards: [ ]
			subtitle: "Swap the casing, swap the tier"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "122EAF728124AE6A"
					item: "create:copper_casing"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "Machines in Every Metal"
			x: 7.0d
			y: 1.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"541D0DC718F4FF4B"
				"6C06A8D2FE2265D4"
			]
			description: [
				"A turning Bellows blows into the block its nozzle faces. A Furnace there, or one standing on a fire there, burns one level hotter, up to &cSearing&r. It never reaches &bBlazing&r, never lights a cold Furnace, and fuel it fans burns twice as fast."
				""
				"That makes low heat go further: a campfire under a fanned Furnace is &6Hot&r with no fuel at all, and lava under one is &cSearing&r. Blowing on a lit campfire, it cooks food twice as fast."
			]
			id: "404A1BD175B2514C"
			rewards: [ ]
			subtitle: "One level hotter"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "1F63B27233C2ED57"
					item: "mcremix:bellows"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "The Bellows"
			x: 1.75d
			y: 1.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"541D0DC718F4FF4B"
				"5CF0F2FE999D2187"
				"3AC9A7994C4F9DC0"
			]
			description: [
				"A Furnace heats a Create boiler standing on it by the fuel burning in it, the way a Blaze Burner does. Fuel burning &cSearing&r boils it as a fed Blaze Burner would; a &eWarm&r or &6Hot&r fire only keeps it simmering. Heat from under the Furnace passes up as it is, so a soul campfire beneath only simmers it."
				""
				"So steam power arrives with Coal Coke, without a trip to the Nether for blazes."
				""
				"Brass, iron and steel have steam engines of their own, and each goes only on tanks of its own metal. Create's engine goes on Create's copper tanks."
			]
			id: "5C2C3A2E77FAA0F8"
			rewards: [ ]
			subtitle: "A Furnace under a boiler"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "394D0CCD3CCC42DC"
					item: "create:steam_engine"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "Steam from Fire"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 3.5d
		}
	]
	subtitle: [
		"Create's kinetics, remixed: supports, materials and their limits"
	]
	title: "Turning"
}
